      "side": 1,
      "message": "`bind_java_type` didn\u0027t exist when I started writing these -- I\u0027ve only just uploaded them, but I actually wrote most of the macros a few months ago. The bindings are relatively new.\n\nThat being said, `bind_java_type` doesn\u0027t support fast / critical native functions -- these are Android-specific additions to JNI that make a significant performance difference but change the shape of the native signature. I\u0027ve got a rework of this patch set to drop the type binding but keep the method registration so we can use this Android-ism. Just cleaning up the CLs, will upload them in the next day or so.\n\nThe actual conversions are a bit more questionable -- they\u0027re mostly proof of concept to show that this work. I\u0027d like to get at least a couple checked in to show that this works, but right now everyone defaults to writing C++ for JNI code and I\u0027d like to make it easier for that to be Rust so getting some examples + build files for it checked in is the primary goal here.",
